  "text": "Pet Oncology Services | Tufts VETS | New England\n525 South Street, Walpole, MA 02081\n(508) 668-5454\nEmail Us\nEmergency & Critical Care Services\n24 hours a day | 7 days a week\nAppointments available Mon-Fri\nAbout\nAbout Tufts VETS\nLocation & Directions\nPhoto Gallery\nOur Blog\nServices\nAnesthesia Services\nCardiology Services\nDermatology & Otology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nOncology Services\nOphthalmology Services\nSurgical Services\nUrgent Care\nEnd-of-Life Services\nStaff\nVeterinarians / Specialists\nClient Services\nAdministrative\nClinical Staff\nReferring Vets\nReferral Policy\nOnline Referral Form\nContinuing Education\nPet Owners\nScheduling & Preparing for a Visit\nHealthy Pet Tips\nQuestions & Answers\nHospital Policies\nHow-to Videos\nClient Forms & Handouts\nTelehealth\nCareCredit Financing\nEmergencies\nOutpatient\nUrgent Care\nCareers\nContact\nBook Urgent Care\nBook Urgent Care\nAbout\nAbout Tufts VETS\nLocation & Directions\nPhoto Gallery\nOur Blog\nServices\nAnesthesia Services\nCardiology Services\nDermatology & Otology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nOncology Services\nOphthalmology Services\nSurgical Services\nUrgent Care\nEnd-of-Life Services\nStaff\nVeterinarians / Specialists\nClient Services\nAdministrative\nClinical Staff\nReferring Vets\nReferral Policy\nOnline Referral Form\nContinuing Education\nPet Owners\nScheduling & Preparing for a Visit\nHealthy Pet Tips\nQuestions & Answers\nHospital Policies\nHow-to Videos\nClient Forms & Handouts\nTelehealth\nCareCredit Financing\nEmergencies\nOutpatient\nUrgent Care\nCareers\nContact\nHome\n/\nServices\n/\nOncology Services\nOncology Services\nThe Tufts VETS Oncology service is dedicated to enhancing and extending the quality of life for our veterinary cancer patients. We offer specialized knowledge in the diagnosis and staging of cancers, development of treatment plans, and administration of chemotherapy. A veterinary oncologist can help your pet by developing treatment plans that incorporate surgery, chemotherapy, radiation therapy and/or immunotherapy. All cancer treatment plans are customized to meet the needs and goals of the individual patient and family.\nDiagnostic and treatment options available includes:\nChemotherapy\nElectrochemotherapy\nImmunotherapy (including Oncept melanoma vaccine)\nAdvanced Imaging (digital radiography, CT, ultrasound)\nAspirates and Cytology\nBone Marrow Evaluation\nBiopsy\nTumor Staging\nNext Generation Sequencing of Tumor Tissue\nPain Management and Other Palliative Care\nCoordination for Oncologic Surgery\nReferral and Coordination for Radiation Therapy\nOur oncologist, Dr. Coffee, works closely with experienced and compassionate veterinary technicians, Jenny, Shelby, and Rachel, as well as other in-hospital specialists to provide comprehensive cancer therapy for each and every patient. We are dedicated to working closely with you and your pet’s primary veterinarian to provide the best possible care.\nAppointments are available Monday through Thursday.\nDepartment Staff\nCalli Coffee, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nPlease browse our other services to learn more about what we offer.\nAnesthesia Services\nCardiology Services\nDermatology & Otology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nOncology Services\nOphthalmology Services\nSurgical Services\nUrgent Care\nEnd-of-Life Services\nTufts VETS\n525 South Street, Walpole, MA 02081\nPhone:\n(508) 668-5454\nFax:\n(508) 850-9809\nEmail:\nEmail Us\nConnect With Us\nContact Us\nSite Map\nHospital Hours\n24 hours a day | 7 days a week\nAppointments available Mon-Fri\nAbout\nServices\nStaff\nReferring Vets\nPet Owners\nEmergencies\nOutpatient\nUrgent Care\nCareers\nContact Us\nVeterinary Website ©\nVetNetwork\n, LLC\n-\nContact VetNetwork",
